description: TILA agent memory — read and append task-history
alwaysApply: true
---

Agents do not remember chats. Prior work lives in `docs/brain/`.

Before a feature task:
1. Read `docs/brain/roadmap.md`, `docs/brain/gaps.md`.
2. Read or create `docs/brain/task-history/<feature-slug>.md` (copy `_TEMPLATE.md`).
3. Prefer `/StartTask` then `/MakePlan` before coding.

After finishing (or when asked to hand off):
1. Append an entry to the task-history file (never rewrite history).
2. Update roadmap/gaps/ADRs if status or decisions changed.
3. Prefer `/Handoff` (after `/ReviewCode` and `/TestCode` when implementing).

Skill: `.agents/skills/tila-memory/SKILL.md`.
